gfs2: Get rid of delayed withdraws

jira KERNEL-1773
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10
commit-author Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
commit 8daf6c2b3d8ceea5559cceb8ed7e1275ee72a7be
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10/8daf6c2b.failed

Now that gfs2_withdraw() is asynchronous, is can be called in any
context and there is no more need for gfs2_withdraw_delayed() or for
turning delayed withdraws into actual withdraws.  Remove the
now-obsolete code.

	Signed-off-by: Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8daf6c2b3d8ceea5559cceb8ed7e1275ee72a7be)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

